ontain test ports or two tightly closing resilient-seated shut-off valves. Dual check valves are not approved for installation as backflow prevention devices.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"36f39920-1739-5f7e-bd0b-c97a8f89f724"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"14.35.490","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/14.35.490","content_hash":"0f6f01b36910bd9cbf425da467e02f40e581295cfbd7d3e54d477272ab2a82c1","heading":null,"ordinal":13,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:14.35.490:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:14.35.490:block:13","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/14.35.490","text":"“Free water surface” means a water surface at atmospheric pressure.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"b40c4d06-ad55-5057-8e14-02784b22114a"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"14.35.490","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/14.35.490","content_hash":"939db88631140684bef61a191d7b41da00fc576dbc94f88ee3cd58ab9703c466","heading":null,"ordinal":14,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:14.35.490:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:14.35.490:block:14","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/14.35.490","text":"“Industrial fluids” means any fluids or solutions that may be chemically, biologically or otherwise contaminated or polluted in a form or concentration that would constitute a health, system, pollution or plumbing hazard if introduced into an approved water supply. This may include, but shall not be limited to, polluted or contaminated waters; all types of processed waters and used waters originating from the public potable water system that may have deteriorated in sanitary quality; chemicals in fluid form; plating acids and alkalis; circulating cooling waters connected to an open cooling tower; or cooling towers that are chemically or biologically treated or stabilized with toxic substances; contaminated natural waters, such as wells, springs, streams, rivers, bays, harbors, seas, irrigation canals or systems, etc.; oils, gases, glycerin, paraffin, caustic and acid solutions; and other liquid and gaseous fluids used in industrial or other purposes, including for firefighting purposes.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"e6e6c15d-0a22-54c5-869e-4d3ccac64806"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"14.35.490","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/14.35.490","content_hash":"a80d35018592b7d73cb7f61a3ae53f913e63505ba6006f9bfeee7986b89b25d5","heading":null,"ordinal":15,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:14.35.490:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:14.35.490:block:15","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/14.35.490","text":"“Isolation” means the appropriate method of backflow prevention within the customer’s potable water system at the point of use.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"1d31b318-3154-5b0e-9908-db69e97833e6"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"14.35.490","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/14.35.490","content_hash":"29dc7062e19a690bc597d14465a02722a3a263b7e349e357f442c6f8406d45ad","heading":null,"ordinal":16,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:14.35.490:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:14.35.490:block:16","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/14.35.490","text":"“K.A.R.” means Kansas Administrative Regulations.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"02947a35-b3ee-53be-a6ae-d52c2fa30e0f"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"14.35.490","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/14.35.490","content_hash":"83